    "title": "Five honored for achievements in Caribbean-American Heritage Month - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ROCHESTER, N.Y. (WROC) — State officials honored Rochester’s local Caribbean-American community during a ceremony at the office of Congressman Joe Morelle. Five honorees received recognition for their contributions and achievements. “This is a big deal,” Honoree Jerome H. Underwood said. “For not only me, but for Caribbean people and as I stand under one of the prettiest flags in the world…” Each honoree was represented with a framed copy of their recognition which Congressman Morelle submitted to the Congressional record which will be available in the House of Representatives in Congress for all time. Caribbean-American Heritage Month is celebrated every June. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to RochesterFirst.",
